.TH BREAKTHROUGH 1 "2026-09-30" "breakthrough" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
breakthrough, brk \- POSIX-friendly, window/menu-based TUI file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B breakthrough
[\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B breakthrough
\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-v\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B breakthrough
is a terminal file manager for Linux system administration, sysops, and
devops work, built with
.B tcell
and
.BR tview .
It favors mouse-friendly window/menu operation and real shell
workflows over reimplementing a shell or cloning Midnight Commander
\-\- every mouse action has a keyboard equivalent, and existing POSIX tools
.RI ( du ", " df ", " find ", " grep ", " sed ", " rsync ", ...)
are used directly wherever their own established behavior is more
useful than a reimplementation.
.PP
.B brk
is a short alias for
.BR breakthrough ,
installed alongside it by the .deb/.rpm packages, and takes the same
arguments.
.PP
Run with no arguments, it opens in the current working directory.
Everything else \-\- keybindings, panels, Look/Edit, archive browsing,
remote (SFTP) connections, Search, batch rename, and the rest \-\- is
documented in the application's own built\-in help
.RB ( ?
key) and the online user guide (see
.B SEE ALSO
below), not repeated here: unlike this options summary, that reference
can never drift out of sync with a running binary, since it ships
inside it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PATH
Open this directory instead of the current working directory. Also
becomes the panel's own "Start" button target for the rest of the
session.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print the version, commit, build date, and builder, then exit without
starting the TUI.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Redirect this process's own stderr \-\- including an uncaught panic and
its full traceback \-\- to a log file for the whole run, instead of it
being lost behind the TUI's alternate screen buffer. See
.B FILES
below for the log's location. Also enables a full, all\-goroutine
traceback (rather than just the panicking one) for the rare panic that
reaches the runtime's own default handler uncaught.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/breakthrough/config
System\-wide default configuration, flat
.I key = value
syntax. Absent unless installed via a
.B .deb
or
.B .rpm
package, which ships a documented starting point there.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/breakthrough/config
(or
.I ~/.config/breakthrough/config
if
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset)
Per\-user configuration, overriding the system\-wide default above.
Created lazily the first time a setting is actually changed from
within the application \-\- absent until then.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/breakthrough/trash
(or
.I ~/.local/share/breakthrough/trash
if
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME
is unset)
Where "Move to Trash" relocates a deleted entry, instead of removing
it outright. Created lazily on first use.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/breakthrough/debug.log
(or
.I ~/.local/state/breakthrough/debug.log
if
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset)
.B \-\-debug's
own log file (see
.B OPTIONS
above).
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation \-\- every keybinding, configuration key, and
feature \-\- lives at
.UR https://github.com/jagottsicher/breakthrough
.UE
and in the application's own built\-in help, opened with the
.B ?
key.
.SH AUTHOR
jagottsicher
